WEBVTT

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Hop, step, jump.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.140
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.950
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.400
Who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.650
They call me calm, strong, and cool. {cool de tsuyoku...}

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.000
Everyone says I'm popular.{iketeru to...}

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.410
But the truth is, I'm not like that at all. {honto wa...}

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.620
I'm just an ordinary girl! {futsuu ni...}

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.730
I wish I could just get rid {puressha nank...}

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:54.510
of all this pressure and be myself. {sunao ni naritai...}

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.350
But they'd all say it's out of character. {kyarajanai toka...}

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.760
Unlock my heart! {atashi no kokoro...}

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.110
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.960
Your Guardian Characters are with you. {shugo kyara ga...}

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.210
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.280
It'll be okay, really! {zenzen...}

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.190
Just be who you wanna be. {naritai...}

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.960
Having only one style would be way too boring. {hitotsu...}

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.220
Just do it the way you wanna do it. {yaritai...}

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.490
You can do anything! {nandatte...}

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.110
I know that...{kitto}

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.950
Hop, step, jump.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.840
Drew, draw, drawn.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.710
Chip, syrup, whip.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.020
...is who I wanna be. {naritai atashi}

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.320
Did you see that drama on TV last night?

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.070
I did! Okashin is so cool! {XXX If this refers to a real person, I wasn't able to figure out who. I assume it's like "Kimutaku" (Kimura Takuya), so I'm just leaving it as Okashin.}

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:58.130
But my dad suddenly got all mad and was like, "What's so great about that show-off?"

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.340
Mine said, "I was a lot cooler than him when I was young!"

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.910
As if, right?

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.500
On the other hand, Amu-chan...

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.180
Really has it made!

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.080
Your dad's a super famous photographer!

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.900
Your mom writes for a cool magazine!

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.950
Your cool family gets to live in a designer condo!

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.410
It's so great! Super stylish!

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.870
I wish my family was like that.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.880
Yeah, I'm so jealous!

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.110
Doesn't your dad take pictures of wild birds?

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.060
And your mom's magazine is <i>Housewife's Wisdom?</i>

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.250
Rumors get bigger as they spread.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.540
Episode 19
Mom and Dad's Memory!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.280
Amu-chan, Ami-chan! Look this way!

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.580
So cute!

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.400
You're the best!

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.610
You both are just too cute!

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.140
You're angels descended from heaven!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.230
Bravo!

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.960
Okay, now look this way. Come on now, face this way.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.710
Sis!

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.870
Push me! Push me!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.250
All right.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.470
I've got that smile!

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.630
Marvelous! Excellent!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.320
Ami-chan, you're the best!

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.210
Good grief, Dad.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:07.640
Really good!

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.250
He's so passionate.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.590
Even more than usual today. Amazing.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.370
Wonderful!

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.380
Dear, should you be taking pictures only of Amu-chan and Ami-chan?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.120
We came here so you could work, didn't we?

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.880
That's right.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.890
What're you doing, Dad?

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.210
Shh!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.370
It's over there.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.330
What're you doing, Dad?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.360
Shh. Look up there.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.610
That's called a Great Spotted Woodpecker.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.470
Dad has a serious side, too.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.140
Doesn't he look dreamy when he's working?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.840
Dweamy!

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.680
I guess.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:22.330
He's pretty cool.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:30.550
Today reminded me of the first time your mom and I went on a date.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.670
We went to a park together.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.110
I was so nervous!

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.020
You tripped five times!

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.160
That's right!

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.060
We ate ice cream together.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:41.930
That's right!

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.290
And after that, we took pictures on the grass!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.700
Right, right!

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.410
You looked lovely in that white one-piece dress.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.460
Right, right! What?

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:55.430
That's not what I was wearing.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.920
Are you mistaking me for someone else?

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.970
No! It's a misunderstanding! A misunderstanding!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.120
Um, you were definitely wearing... um... um...

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.780
You don't remember, do you?!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.420
You're always like this!

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:13.960
You don't have to get so angry about it!

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.200
But you always forget the things that matter.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.880
Like when you-

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.790
Fine! I'll run away!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.000
He said he'd run away, but he went into the house.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.050
Huh? Where's Dad?

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:29.400
Who cares? {not lit}

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:31.850
Huh?

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.600
I won't open it.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.680
I'm running away!

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.900
That's not running away.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.000
Omelets!

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.770
Thank you!

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.780
Hold on a minute.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:57.460
Dear, dinner is ready.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.600
Dinner...

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.380
That won't work! You can't tempt me with food!

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:07.280
I'm not the kind of man who can be enticed by such things!

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:07.670
Oh, really? But I made your favorite fluffy omelets.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.180
Fluffy omelets!

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.320
It's so fluffy.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:20.350
About earlier, I was in the wrong, too. I apologize.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:26.050
So do I! I ran away, even though it was my fault!

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.390
Come on, let's all have dinner together.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.370
Okay.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.480
Was that running away?

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.010
I dunno.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:40.470
You make the best omelets in the world.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:45.510
You know, to commemorate our reconciliation, we should get that picture out.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.560
You mean the picture that was taken when we first met?

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.790
That's the one!

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:51.960
Great idea!

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.950
A picture from the first time you met?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:57.810
That's right. That picture holds precious memories for us.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:04.490
It comes from a time when I was young and working part-time at a publisher's.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:09.450
Back then, my dream was to become a journalist.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.840
Things weren't going very well at all, though.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:18.330
"Maybe I should just give up on my dream,"

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.740
is what I kept thinking.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.830
You're wonderful! You sparkle!

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.090
Here!

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:38.990
U-Um...

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.790
B-Bye.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.050
I said it! I really said it!

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.320
He's a strange one.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.880
All right, I'll keep trying!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:01.990
A little while after that came our fateful reunion.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.210
Really?

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:11.900
I was able to realize my dream of becoming a journalist because of your father's encouragement.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.530
So the picture is the one Dad took that day?

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.110
Yes! I keep it in this album.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.990
Oh, but I was looking at it earlier and I put it inside a copy of <i>Wild Birds Monthly.</i>

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.640
<i>Wild Birds Monthly?</i>

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:27.190
Yeah, right here.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.330
Oh no, the <i>Wild Birds Monthly?</i> is gone!

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.020
Didn't you take that one to the bazaar yesterday?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.530
I-I did!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.810
Why would you do that without checking inside first?

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.690
It's your fault for putting important stuff in there!

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:47.760
You're just too careless! Like when you carelessly ate my pudding!

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.380
You should talk! You used my toothbrush!

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.070
That was just a mistake!

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:57.270
I don't believe you! That's not possible! Yours is blue and mine is pink!

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.400
They've moved on to completely unrelated things now.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.850
Color aside, they're exactly the same!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.700
Really.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.580
Please stop fighting!

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.670
This is so like you!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:07.150
I've had enough! I'm running away!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.360
He went in the bathroom again.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.320
Seriously, that's not running away.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.070
You can just leave him alone in there. He's so...

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:30.390
That picture means so much to me.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:33.290
Mom.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.890
Amu-chan, let's go look for it!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.640
Yeah, Sis!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:40.530
Ami.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:42.840
It might not've been sold yet.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:48.310
Your parents will be so sad if their precious picture is lost.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:53.040
True. Mom, where's that bazaar being held?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.560
In the central park, but I'm sure it's too late.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:58.930
We won't know if we don't go!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:02.570
Amu-chan. You're right.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:05.210
I'm gonna help, too!

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:08.980
You should stay home, Ami. You might get lost or something.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.960
What? No!

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.770
Ami-chan, please take care of your dad for me.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.800
No! No! No! { These continue in the background}

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.620
This is a mission that only you carry out!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:20.320
A mission onwy I can do?

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.580
That's right!

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.480
Roger!

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:26.130
All right, let's go!

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:27.730
Yeah!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.380
Poor me.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.180
It's so crowded here.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:54.700
It's too early to give up, though.

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.100
Amu-chan!

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.600
Huh? I thought I heard Nadeshiko's voice.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.540
Over here! Over here!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.460
Yaya.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:06.130
Nadeshiko, Yaya, and Baya-san, too?

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.270
What're you doing?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.460
We are selling items here at the city bazaar.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.350
Yaya and I are helping Baya.

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.820
Yeah!

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:20.260
This is the ultra-rare Baya Collection.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:21.360
Wow...

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:23.290
What's this?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:28.400
For some reason, the hair on that doll gets longer and longer.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:33.310
Look, I tried putting some stuff out, too.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:38.050
But they're totally not selling.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.160
That's not surprising.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.080
Amu-chan, are you shopping?

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:44.840
No, I'm sort of looking for something.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.500
Looking for something?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.280
Man, it's noisy today-nya!

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.180
I can't even take a nice walk-nya.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.300
It looks like they're selling a bunch of stuff-nya.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.660
Maybe there's an Embryo here!

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:03.780
Nah, there's no way.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.360
What are they doing here-nya?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:09.170
Could they be looking for the Embryo?

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:12.630
I can't let them out of my sight-nya! After them-nya!

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.320
Thank you very much!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.250
Excuse me.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.640
Oh, Hinamori-san, hello.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.930
Do you still have any of the things that I brought?

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:29.810
Specifically, in a cardboard box full of magazines, one called <i>Wild Birds Monthly</i>.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.330
Oh, that? It's already been sold.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:36.130
It has? Oh no...

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:37.570
Mom?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.600
We were too late. It's been sold.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:41.760
What?

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:45.440
Excuse me, do you remember what the person who bought the magazine looked like?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:51.640
It was a boy with glasses, I believe. He said he liked wild birds. {lit is a quote ("I like wild birds")}

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:54.020
A boy wearing glasses?

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:58.700
Mom, let's look for that boy and ask him just to give us the picture back.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.040
But...

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.460
He might still be here.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:06.460
But there are so many people here we'll never find him.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:10.320
We will. Let's just do what we can.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:12.640
Amu-chan.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:16.200
The bazaar is big, so let's split up and search.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.150
Yeah!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.990
Nadeshiko, Yaya.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:23.430
Okay, we'll meet in an hour in front of the clock tower at the edge of the park!

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:24.030
Okay.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:25.170
Got it.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:32.660
A boy with glasses.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.610
A boy with glasses.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.930
Glasses.

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.090
Glasses.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.540
Glasses.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.600
Amu-chan!

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:42.780
Hey!

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.450
You there!

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:50.600
H-Hinamori-senpai!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:56.960
To see you on a weekend and to have you call out to me...

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.480
W-What's going on?

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.290
I'm just too happy!

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:04.640
Um, did you buy any copies of <i>Wild Birds Monthly</i> here today?

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.000
How did you know?

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:07.210
So you did!

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:11.520
She cares enough to know that much about me!

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:15.010
I'm so happy I could die!

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:17.170
Let me see that magazine!

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.340
Well done-nya!

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:27.340
Does this magazine contain the secret of the Embryo-nya?

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.730
Yoru!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.230
Give that back!

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:34.350
No, it's mine-nya!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:35.420
Wait!

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:38.850
Hey! Wait!

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:42.210
Hinamori-senpai. Even the way she leaves is "cool & spicy!"

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.790
Ami-chan.

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.920
Is your mom back yet?

00:14:54.990 --> 00:15:00.050
Not yet, but I'm standing guard until she comes back!

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:08.620
The Embryo isn't in this, but it is full of tasty pictures-nya.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.380
Jeez, where'd that Yoru run off to?

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.330
Amu-chan, over there!

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:18.060
So that's where he is!

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.300
Amu-chan, Character Change!

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.890
Right!

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.110
Hop!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.190
Step!

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:27.030
Jump!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.410
Give it back, Yoru!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.100
Wait!

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:40.000
Give it back, you thieving cat!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.540
Being told to give something back makes me not want to-nya!

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.280
Wait!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.830
Amu-chi!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.520
I wonder what they're doing.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:49.520
W-Wait!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.570
Is that magazine...

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.750
It might be!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.800
Yaya-chan, let's Character Change, too.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:57.750
Yeah!

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:58.760
Pretty!

00:15:58.790 --> 00:15:59.950
Cutie!

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.670
Love Baby!

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.660
Chin! Ton! Shan!

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:12.400
You gonna give that back, dumbass? {starts with "sono hon"}

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:17.630
Gigantic Rattle Attack!

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.200
What're they doing-nya?

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.480
My chance!

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.700
What're you doing-nya?

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:33.990
Give it back! Even if it's just the picture inside!

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:35.140
I don't wanna-nya!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.830
Give it back!

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.580
I got it!

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.000
Are you okay, Amu-chan?

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.380
That looked painful.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:58.070
I'll let you get away today-nya!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.010
Never come back, you jerk!

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.410
Ouch.

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:04.570
Amu-chan, are you okay?

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:05.640
I'm fine.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:06.760
And the picture?

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.010
I've got it.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.540
But it's all ripped.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:15.660
What'll we do, Amu-chan?

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:18.810
We have to do something about the clock tower, too.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.510
We're sorry.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:21.970
What should I do?

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:23.830
Amu-chan.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:24.610
Su.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:27.800
If you need something fixed, leave it to me.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:31.210
If you do a Character Transformation with me, it will all be okay.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:32.180
Oh yeah!

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:37.240
My heart: Unlock!

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:19.040
Character Transformation: Amulet Clover!

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.030
Here we go, Amu-chan.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:28.340
There!

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:35.550
Let's gently fix everything and put them back the way they were.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:39.140
Remake Honey!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.780
So this is Mom and Dad's treasure.

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:02.600
Amu-chan.

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:03.930
Mom!

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:06.130
I didn't find it.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.510
Here!

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:08.620
Isn't this it?

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:17.740
Yes. Thank you so much, Amu-chan!

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:19.360
Too tight!

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.160
Thank goodness.

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:21.940
Yeah.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.830
I'm touched.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.900
Dear, you don't have to cry anymore.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.420
But I'm just so happy!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.910
My goodness, you've always been such a crybaby.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.600
Amu-chan, thank you!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.910
It's no big deal.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:46.070
You're so cool!

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:51.390
But Dad, why did you talk to Mom when she was looking so depressed?

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:54.100
Oh, that's because...

00:19:56.510 --> 00:20:01.810
At that time, it was my dream to become a wild bird photographer.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.810
But no matter how many times I tried to sell my pictures,

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.660
it didn't work out.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:12.810
That's when I saw your mom working so hard.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:25.570
She shone more brilliantly than anyone else.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:31.120
When I saw her, I knew I had to keep trying, too.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:38.340
So when I saw that she was feeling down, I just had to give her something,

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:42.780
just like she had shared her motivation with me.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:54.030
I was able to become a wild bird photographer because of her.

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:57.650
So you knew about me before we even met?

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.960
I was so embarrassed that I couldn't talk to you.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:02.650
Oh, Darling!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.450
Dear!

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:05.070
Darling!

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:12.230
If Mom and Dad had dreams, they must've had hearts' eggs, too.

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:18.480
They raised them carefully, got married, and then Ami and I were born.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:19.780
Dear.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.080
Darling.

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:26.400
Your mom and dad are wonderful, aren't they?

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.280
Yeah.

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:31.460
I'm the luckiest guy in the world because I got to marry you!

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:36.210
And I also get to be Amu-chan and Ami-chan's father, two cute girls who look just like me!

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:41.230
Excuse me? They're so cute because they take after <i>me</i>, not you.

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:43.450
No, they look just like me.

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:46.890
No, they don't!

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.860
Their cuteness comes from me!

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:46.730
They're fighting again.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.540
And over something so stupid.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.980
Amu-chan and Ami-chi look just like me!

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:51.400
Fighting is bad.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:51.540
If it came from you, they wouldn't be nearly as lovely!

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:56.320
I'm going to run away!

00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:58.570
To the bathroom again?

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:06.420
Occupied!

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:14.800
This time for sure, I'm really and truly going to run away!

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:16.820
To the bathtub this time?

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:41.390
Unless the world ends, I'll always {sekai ga...}

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:44.160
love you!  Yeah, you! {suki da yo...}

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:47.630
'Cause I just love, love, love you! {suki suki suki...}

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:52.360
Sure, I might struggle, but I'm still living. {jitabata...}

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:55.040
So figure it out already! Yeah, you! {kizukeyo...}

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.680
Even though I love, love, love you, {suki suki suki...}

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:04.870
I wanna say it but, shoot, I just can't! {iitaikuseni...}

00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:08.990
I wanna show you what's in my heart! {tsutaetai...}

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:12.420
Oh yes! You're my one true hero. {oh yes!...}

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:17.580
Being in love's gonna be a bumpy ride.  {koishiterukagiri...}

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:23.510
But keep going! Okay, greenhorn rider? {hashitsuzukero...}

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:28.760
Straight down the path, into the sunset, stronger and stronger. {yuuyake...}

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:37.630
Ride through the wild land of youth. {seishun no...}

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:56.130
A present! A present! Give her a present!

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:58.980
What's with that strange song, you guys?

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:01.010
Amu-chan, what kind of present would you give?

00:24:01.060 --> 00:24:02.150
To who?

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:04.450
To the person you care about!

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:09.270
Oh, I see. Well, I guess I'd give, um...

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:12.290
Next time on Shugo Chara: A Gift For You!

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.500
What in the world will Kukai-kun give as a gift?

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:19.410
What? Kukai's giving a present? To who?

00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:24.330
Tune in Next Time!
